  "body": "## What changed\n\nKeep Sodick constant taper refused until its mapping preserves the generated wire path.\nRefuse WireAngle records by operation name even when the section omits WireTaper.\nStop cutting that section instead of silently writing a vertical move.\nRecord the evidence and rejected mappings in docs/decisions/1496-sodick-taper.md.\nThis uses the issue's allowed outcome of documenting the mapping limits and retaining refusal.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe post ignored WireAngle records.\nA direct angle-word stream without WireTaper could therefore emit a vertical cut without a warning.\nLower-guide XY and explicit upper-guide offsets cannot simply become nominal A angles without proving the corner and transition motion.\nThe alternative angle stream uses work-relative WirePlane, which does not establish Sodick's table-relative program height.\n\nSodick's [2012 LN1W/LN2W training manual](https://fab.cba.mit.edu/content/tools/sodick_edm/sodick_user_manual_small.pdf), printed pages 66-70, describes G51/G52, A, G50 and the table/guide settings.\nThat newer-control source does not prove the complete mapping for this post's Mark 21/EX21 target.\nUnconfirmed items are Mark 21/EX21 TP/TN initialization and datum/calibration correspondence, corner and lead/cancel interpolation, and the signed angle mapping in that frame.\nNo unconfirmed words are emitted.\n\n## Tests\n\n`sodick_refuses_angle_words_even_without_section_taper` fails on the original post and passes with the guard.\nIt covers positive, negative and zero angles.\n`sodick_vertical_stream_still_posts_without_angle_words` preserves vertical posting.\nMutation: restoring assets/posts/sodick-wire.cps from upstream/main makes the refusal pin fail again.\nRestoring the fix makes both pins pass.\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passes the selected post and app suites.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical Sodick control was exercised.\nNo tapered output or tapered golden is added.\nThe targeted Mark 21/EX21 mapping remains unverified.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone found for the changed files.\n\nEffort: high.\n\nChangelog: Refuse unsupported Sodick angle-word moves instead of silently posting them vertically; retain taper refusal pending a verified mapping.\n\nFixes #1496\n",
